# Offline Study App — Project Plan

## The Idea
An Android app that fetches study content from the internet while the
student is on WiFi, stores it on the device, and lets them browse it
offline — like a personal, offline mini-internet for studying.

## The Vision
An app that **learns** what a student studies and automatically builds
them a personal offline library — before they even ask.

## Who It's For
University and college students with:
- Campus WiFi but limited/expensive mobile data
- Spotty connectivity at home or on commutes
- Heavy reading/research needs (articles, papers, videos)

## The Problem It Solves
- Students lose access to study material when offline
- Data is expensive
- Existing tools (Pocket, Chrome) are manual and not student-focused

## What Makes It Different
- Automatic fetching on WiFi
- Student-first organization (courses, exams)
- In-app browser that learns from reading behavior
- Everything in one offline library (articles, PDFs, videos, notes)

