## Tech Stack (planned)
- Language: Kotlin
- UI: Jetpack Compose
- Local DB: Room
- File storage: Internal storage
- Background: WorkManager (WiFi-triggered)
- Fetching: OkHttp + Jsoup
- Reader: WebView

## Legal Guardrails
- Save only content the user explicitly chooses
- Respect robots.txt
- Store locally only (no re-sharing content)
- Never bulk-download paid/paywalled content
- Never scrape LMS platforms (Canvas/Moodle) — ToS violation
- Add in-app disclaimer: "For personal offline reading only"
- Video: only open/educational sources (Khan Academy, MIT OCW, teacher-shared)

## How the App Learns (Without Spying)
Android apps cannot see what users do in Chrome (sandboxing).
So the app learns from:
1. Content shared to it from other apps
2. Reading inside its own in-app browser (WebView)
3. Patterns in the user's saved library

